  "notes": "The provincial cultural register records a 3.25 m entrance gate, an open 16.25 by 12.40 m receiving pavilion, the narrow transition wing, a clay-tile main hall, a two-storey secretary wing and the eastern 20 by 21 m three-tier arts pavilion with a south entrance projection. The current public-domain Qualla photo shows the red tile, white piers and deep, sloped roof tiers behind the street frontage."
